  "description": "The primitives Rask's generated wire codecs are written against: reflection-free `Utf8JsonReader`/`Utf8JsonWriter` helpers with one well-worded error per shape mismatch, plus the file carriers a message uses in each direction (`RemoteFile` up, `FileDownload` down). Shared by Rask.Cqrs and Rask.Api so a codec reads the same on either wire and neither package has to depend on the other. Also home to the unit literals every Rask app reads without an import — `3.Seconds`, `50.Megabytes`, `3.Days.Ago`. No reflection, no assembly scanning: publishes clean under the WASM/AOT trimmer.",
